  "summary": "Gitea creates server-side Git hook directories and scripts with mode 0777 and relies on the process umask to restrict…",
  "details": "Gitea creates server-side Git hook directories and scripts with mode 0777 and relies on the process umask to restrict access. With a permissive umask such as 0000 or 0002, another local user who can reach the repository storage may modify a hook or add an executable to a writable hook directory. A later Git operation can execute that file as the Gitea service account.",
  "severity": [
    {
      "type": "CVSS_V3",
